From b4c865d42725ac90b45c5fa0a386249314b1a6ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Jun 2026 12:48:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03984/11362] [outer-loop] Fix code-only scope regression
 caught by adversarial verification: refactor() must keep reasoning

The adversarial verification (workflow verify-goal-repair-and-default-on) found a real medium-severity
defect in the prior default-ON commit: the code-only gate keyed on `"is_level_complete" in required`,
but BOTH induce() and refactor() route through _gen_to_file with that tuple -> flipping default-ON
also forced refactor() (a REASONING task that debugs BEFORE/PREDICTED/OBSERVED mismatches) into the
"skip all reasoning" code-only path. The "induce-scoped, refactor untouched" claim was false.

Fix: thread an explicit `codeonly_eligible` flag through _gen_to_file -> generate(); induce() sets
True, refactor() sets False. The gate is now `(env != "0") and codeonly_eligible and "is_level_complete"
in required`, so refactor and gap-fillers are genuinely untouched. (This also corrects the original
env-gated behaviour, which over-applied to refactor when enabled.)

Tests: new tests/python/test_codeonly_induce_scoping.py (5 tests: induce eligible -> directive+stop;
not-eligible -> normal /no_think, no stop; opt-out=0 disables; induce()/refactor() method-level
routing) + a round-2-repair-on-refactor test added to test_goal_repair_degenerate_predicate.py (the
other coverage gap the verification flagged). 22 tests pass; ruff clean.

Adversarial verification confirmed the goal-repair loop CANNOT fabricate a solve (the loose fallback
is only a search bias; the real level-up is decided by the real-env frame + the offline reproduction
gate, neither of which consult the goal predicate). Known minor (deferred): when repaired,
goal_predicate_satisfiable reports the FALLBACK's satisfiability; traceable via rounds[].goal_repaired.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
